Description:
    Estimates provider-specific empirical null distributions whose centers can
    depend on provider case-mix summaries and whose variances can depend on
    effective provider size. Includes Gaussian models, a Poisson-lognormal
    exact-moment working null, unified post-model provider tests and intervals,
    fixed and robust groupwise calibration, and diagnostics for weak
    identification and unstable calibration. The estimated parameters describe
    a provider-level null fingerprint and do not identify a latent patient-level
    confounder or its causal decomposition. For background, see Hartman et al.
    (2024) <doi:10.1214/23-aoas1809>.
